  "title": "The NIMH Healthy Research Volunteer Dataset",
  "description": "A large-scale dataset characterizing healthy research volunteers recruited at the NIMH intramural program. It combines clinical assessments, mood psychometrics, neuropsychological and cognitive testing, structural and functional MRI, diffusion imaging, and a comprehensive MEG battery. Data are shared in BIDS format to support investigations of normal cognition and mood regulation.",
  "methods_description": "Volunteers completed online pre-screening questionnaires, then an in-person screening with a history and physical exam, SCID-5, and KBIT-2. Optional MRI sessions used a protocol initially based on ADNI-3 and later modified to include ABCD elements, alongside NIH Toolbox Cognition Battery tasks. Optional MEG sessions were also acquired, and blood samples were banked for future genetic analysis.",
